# Ownership of the policy system.
#
# CodeRabbit reads `.coderabbit.yaml` from the pull request's own branch, so a
# pull request can in principle weaken the rules it is about to be judged by.
# These entries are what stops that: with "Require review from Code Owners"
# enabled on `main`, such a change cannot merge without an Architect, which is
# stronger than any warning the review itself could print.
#
# Deliberately narrow. This file claims the policy system and the architecture
# document it judges against — not the repository.

/.coderabbit.yaml                    @sequentech/Architects
/.github/policies/                   @sequentech/Architects
/.github/CODEOWNERS                  @sequentech/Architects
/.github/workflows/policy-alert.yml  @sequentech/Architects

# The architecture document, for the same reason.
#
# `60-architectural-changes.md` requires a change to update this file. That
# obligation is only as strong as the file: if the record can be rewritten to
# match whatever just merged, "the change must update the document" costs
# nothing. This entry is what makes updating it a decision rather than a
# formality.
/docs/docusaurus/docs/engineering/architecture.md  @sequentech/Architects
